// core/worldmap.js — WorldMap: the world's countries as drawn shapes, for Region Blocks' map (J153, `ddjp_729`)
//
// THE OWNER'S WORDS (`main/01-project.md` item 9): "id also like to see a map of earth with countries in green or red with map
// that light up depending on availability and it also says what country it is as you put your mouse over them". The pop-up
// that draws it is `ui/playlists.js` (its map, `_geoMap`); this file is only the shapes.
//
// ── WHAT THE DATA IS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Natural Earth's 1:110m countries (public domain), as the `world-atlas` package (ISC), version 2.0.2, ships them
// (`countries-110m.json`). Antarctica is left out, so the map is shorter. The projection is Natural Earth's own
// (`d3-geo` 3.1.2, `geoNaturalEarth1`), fitted to 952 units across and moved 4 units in from the top-left, so the whole map is
// 960 × 423 with a 4-unit margin. Each shape is an SVG path in whole units: the projected numbers were cut to one decimal, then
// each rounded to a whole number (half to even), exactly as the approved design page drew them. No map library runs here.
//
// ── HOW EACH SHAPE IS NAMED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// By the country table's number (`core/countries.js`, ISO 3166-1 numeric): Natural Earth's id is that number, so the code is
// the table's, never one written here. Three shapes have no number the table knows — Northern Cyprus, Somaliland and Kosovo —
// so their code is empty, they carry Natural Earth's own name, and the map draws them as "No data". At this scale French Guiana
// is part of France's shape, so it is drawn as France is; the lists still name it on its own (its code is in the table).
// Countries too small for this scale have no shape at all and are in the lists only.
//
// ── HOW TO MAKE IT AGAIN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// With `world-atlas` 2.0.2, `topojson-client` 3.1.0 and `d3-geo` 3.1.2 (npm, outside this tree): read `countries-110m.json`,
// `topojson.feature(world, world.objects.countries)`, drop id "010"; `geoNaturalEarth1().fitWidth(952, those)`, its bounds'
// top-left moved to (4, 4), the height their height rounded up plus 8; each feature's `geoPath`, every number's digits after
// the first decimal dropped, then rounded half to even to a whole unit; the code by `parseInt(id, 10)` against this table's
// numbers. `check-world-map` holds the result: every code the table's or empty, none twice, no Antarctica, every number whole
// and inside the frame.
//
// Pure data: no dependencies, no I/O, no clock. Loaded with the page, as the country table is.

